-- Canada Pension Plan Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-8), Part II from section 55.2(5.2) to section 66.1 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: the individual to whom the law is applied -- a worker, self-employed person, survivor, child or person with
-- a disability who contributes to or may claim from the Canada Pension Plan -- here asking how much a benefit is,
-- whether and when it is payable, what they must do or tell the Minister, and what can be done to them.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules of the cp4 modules imported above as the questions that person asks. Nothing here is
-- new law. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, a list of numbers) -- one for each fact
-- the person can state -- with an @desc worded as the person would be asked; the records and the optional values
-- the modules expect are built inside each question from those answers, and the module rule is then called. No rule
-- is restated. Amounts the Act takes from sections outside this piece (the Pension Index, the portions of the
-- retirement pension, the earnings) are asked as amounts the person can read on the Minister's statement.
--
-- Where the answer may be "the Act does not say" the question returns a MAYBE value: NOTHING then means the
-- Act, as read here, gives no answer, and never zero or "no".
--
-- A judgment the Act hands to the Minister ("if the Minister is satisfied", "in the Minister's opinion") is asked as
-- a fact: has the Minister been satisfied? The prescribed things (the manner of an application, the interval for
-- cancelling a benefit) that the Regulations fix are built into the rule where the module cites the regulation; the
-- Pension Index is asked as a list of numbers because the Act builds the flat rate benefits year on year.
--
-- Every question is grouped under a heading in the order of the Act. A group that only arises in a situation the
-- person may not be in says so in its heading's comment, so that a form can first ask "Has this happened to you?".
--
-- The Pension Index list: "the Pension Index for 1986, then for each later year in order, up to the year in
-- question". The list begins with 1986; the flat rate benefits of sections 56(2), 58(1.1), 59(1) and 59.2 each run
-- from a fixed amount in their own first year.

§ `Canada Pension Plan -- the individual's questions, Part II from section 55.2(5.2) to section 66.1`

§§ `Dividing earnings with a former spouse or partner (section 55.2 from subsection 5.2) -- ask only if you and a spouse or common-law partner have had, or applied for, a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings`

-- s 55.2(5.2). The second additional earnings of both persons for the years they lived together are added and divided equally.
@export What second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings are attributed to me on the division (s 55.2(5.2))?
GIVEN `my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the years we lived together` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period you lived together, in dollars?
      `my former spouse's or partner's second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for those years` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your spouse's or common-law partner's second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the same period, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings are attributed to me on the division` IS
    `s 55.2(5.2) — the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to each person` `my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the years we lived together` `my former spouse's or partner's second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for those years`

-- s 55.2(6), (6.1), (6.2). Where earnings were divided both under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan, the two attributions add up.
@export What are my total unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year of division where a provincial plan also divided them (s 55.2(6), (6.1), (6.2))?
GIVEN `which earnings` IS A Tier @desc Which earnings: the base tier, the first additional tier or the second additional tier?
      `earnings were divided under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were your earnings of this kind divided both under section 55.1 of the Act and under a provincial pension plan?
      `earnings attributed to me under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What earnings of this kind were attributed to you under the Act's division, in dollars?
      `earnings attributed to me under the provincial plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What earnings of this kind were attributed to you under the provincial pension plan's division, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my total unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year of division where a provincial plan also divided them` IS
    CONSIDER `which earnings`
    WHEN `the base tier` THEN `s 55.2(6) — the total base unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` `earnings were divided under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan` `earnings attributed to me under the Act` `earnings attributed to me under the provincial plan`
    WHEN `the first additional tier` THEN `s 55.2(6.1) — the total first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` `earnings were divided under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan` `earnings attributed to me under the Act` `earnings attributed to me under the provincial plan`
    WHEN `the second additional tier` THEN `s 55.2(6.2) — the total second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` `earnings were divided under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan` `earnings attributed to me under the Act` `earnings attributed to me under the provincial plan`

-- s 55.2(7). No division is made for a month of cohabitation in which either person contributed to a provincial plan, unless that plan divides in a substantially similar way.
@export Is the division barred for a month because one of us contributed to a provincial pension plan (s 55.2(7))?
GIVEN `we lived together in the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you and your spouse or common-law partner live together in the month (as the regulations determine months of cohabitation)?
      `one of us contributed to a provincial pension plan for the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did either of you contribute to a provincial pension plan for that month?
      `the provincial plan divides in a substantially similar manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provincial pension plan divide the earnings attributed under it, for that month, in a manner substantially similar to the Act's division?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the division barred for a month because one of us contributed to a provincial pension plan` IS
    `s 55.2(7) — no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` `we lived together in the month` `one of us contributed to a provincial pension plan for the month` `the provincial plan divides in a substantially similar manner`

-- s 55.2(8), (8.1), (8.2). No division is made for a year of low earnings, for months before either person was 18 or after either was 70, for months in which either was getting a retirement pension, or (base earnings only) for months excluded for disability.
@export Is no division of my earnings to be made for this month (s 55.2(8), (8.1), (8.2))?
GIVEN `which earnings` IS A Tier @desc Which earnings: the base tier, the first additional tier or the second additional tier?
      `the month` IS A DATE @desc Which month of your time together are you asking about (any date in it)?
      `our total earnings of this kind for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your and your spouse's or partner's earnings of this kind, together, for the year that includes that month, in dollars? (Not needed for the second additional tier; enter 0)
      `the Year's Basic Exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Year's Basic Exemption for that year, in dollars? (Not needed for the second additional tier; enter 0)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `my former spouse's or partner's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your spouse's or common-law partner's date of birth?
      `one of us was getting a retirement pension in the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was either of you a beneficiary of a retirement pension under the Act or a provincial pension plan in that month?
      `the month is excluded for disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that month excluded from either of your contributory periods by reason of disability? (Only the base tier asks; otherwise enter no)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is no division of my earnings to be made for this month` IS
    CONSIDER `which earnings`
    WHEN `the base tier` THEN `s 55.2(8) — no division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` `the month` `our total earnings of this kind for the year` `the Year's Basic Exemption for the year` `my date of birth` `my former spouse's or partner's date of birth` `one of us was getting a retirement pension in the month` `the month is excluded for disability`
    WHEN `the first additional tier` THEN `s 55.2(8.1) — no division of first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` `the month` `our total earnings of this kind for the year` `the Year's Basic Exemption for the year` `my date of birth` `my former spouse's or partner's date of birth` `one of us was getting a retirement pension in the month`
    WHEN `the second additional tier` THEN `s 55.2(8.2) — no division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` `the month` `my date of birth` `my former spouse's or partner's date of birth` `one of us was getting a retirement pension in the month`

-- s 55.2(9). After a division the adjusted benefit is paid from the following month; a benefit not payable without the division is not paid for the month of the division or before.
@export From which month is my adjusted benefit paid after the division (s 55.2(9))?
GIVEN `the month in which the division takes place` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the division take place (any date in it)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From which month is my adjusted benefit paid after the division` IS
    `s 55.2(9) — the month from which the adjusted benefit is paid` `the month in which the division takes place`

@export Can a benefit that was not payable without the division be paid to me for this month (s 55.2(9))?
GIVEN `the month for which payment is in question` IS A DATE @desc For which month are you asking whether payment can be made (any date in it)?
      `the month in which the division takes place` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the division take place (any date in it)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a benefit that was not payable without the division be paid to me for this month` IS
    `s 55.2(9) — a benefit that was not payable without the division can be paid for the month` `the month for which payment is in question` `the month in which the division takes place`

-- s 55.2(10). Both persons, or their estates, are notified of the division.
@export Must I and my former spouse or partner be notified of the division (s 55.2(10))?
GIVEN `there is a division under section 55.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I and my former spouse or partner be notified of the division` IS
    `s 55.2(10) — both persons subject to the division, or their estates, must be notified` `there is a division under section 55.1`

§§ `Applying late because of incapacity (section 55.3) -- ask only if you were unable to apply for a division, or to give the information, when you should have`

-- s 55.3(1), (3), (4). If you were incapable of forming or expressing an intention to apply on the day you actually applied, the Minister may treat the application as made in the first month a division could have taken place, or the month your last period of incapacity began, whichever is later.
@export Can the Minister treat my division application as made earlier because I was incapable when I applied (s 55.3(1), (3), (4))?
GIVEN `the last day I was incapacitated` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day on which you were incapacitated? (The section covers only people incapacitated on or after 1 January 1991.)
      `my incapacity was one continuous period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your period of incapacity one continuous period?
      `a regulation allows an interrupted period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a regulation allow a period of incapacity that was not continuous?
      `the Minister is satisfied I was incapable on the day I applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied, on evidence you or someone for you provided, that you were incapable of forming or expressing an intention to apply on the day your application was actually made?
      `the first month a division could have taken place` IS A DATE @desc In which month could a division first have taken place (any date in it)?
      `the month my last period of incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the Minister consider your last relevant period of incapacity to have begun (any date in it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Can the Minister treat my division application as made earlier because I was incapable when I applied` IS
    `s 55.3(1) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received` `the last day I was incapacitated` `my incapacity was one continuous period` `a regulation allows an interrupted period` `the Minister is satisfied I was incapable on the day I applied` `the first month a division could have taken place` `the month my last period of incapacity began`

-- s 55.3(2), (3), (4). If you were incapable before the day you applied but had stopped being incapable, and you applied within the window the section allows, the Minister may treat the application as made earlier.
@export Can the Minister treat my division application as made earlier because I was incapable until shortly before I applied (s 55.3(2), (3), (4))?
GIVEN `the last day I was incapacitated` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day on which you were incapacitated? (The section covers only people incapacitated on or after 1 January 1991.)
      `my incapacity was one continuous period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your period of incapacity one continuous period?
      `a regulation allows an interrupted period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a regulation allow a period of incapacity that was not continuous?
      `the Minister is satisfied I was incapable earlier and had stopped being incapable before I applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied, on evidence you or someone for you provided, that you were incapable of forming or expressing an intention to apply before the day you applied, and had stopped being incapable before that day?
      `the day I stopped being incapable` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you stop being incapable?
      `the days of my incapacity` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days did your period of incapacity last?
      `the day I actually applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your application actually made or the information actually received?
      `the first month a division could have taken place` IS A DATE @desc In which month could a division first have taken place (any date in it)?
      `the month my last period of incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the Minister consider your last relevant period of incapacity to have begun (any date in it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Can the Minister treat my division application as made earlier because I was incapable until shortly before I applied` IS
    `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` `the last day I was incapacitated` `my incapacity was one continuous period` `a regulation allows an interrupted period` `the Minister is satisfied I was incapable earlier and had stopped being incapable before I applied` `the day I stopped being incapable` `the days of my incapacity` `the day I actually applied` `the first month a division could have taken place` `the month my last period of incapacity began`
§§ `Disability pension (section 56) -- ask only if you are disabled, or may become disabled, within the meaning of the Act`

-- s 56(5). The contributory period used for the average runs from January 1966 or your 18th birthday, whichever is later, to the month you are determined to have become disabled, less months excluded for disability and (for benefits after 1977) months of low earnings while receiving a family allowance.
@export How many months are in my contributory period for a disability pension (s 56(5))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the month I was determined to have become disabled` IS A DATE @desc In which month were you determined to have become disabled for the purposes of the disability pension (any date in it)?
      `the month for which the benefit is payable` IS A DATE @desc For which month is the benefit payable (any date in it)?
      `months excluded because of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months were excluded from your contributory period under the Act or a provincial plan by reason of disability?
      `months of a family allowance with low earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months were you a family allowance recipient in a year in which your base unadjusted pensionable earnings were no more than your basic exemption?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months are in my contributory period for a disability pension` IS
    `s 56(5) — the number of months in the contributory period` `my date of birth` `the month I was determined to have become disabled` `the month for which the benefit is payable` `months excluded because of disability` `months of a family allowance with low earnings`

-- s 56(2). The flat rate benefit is $91.06 for a benefit starting in 1986, 233.38 times the Pension Index ratio for 1987, and the previous year's amount times the ratio after that.
@export What is the flat rate part of my disability pension (s 56(2))?
GIVEN `the year my disability pension starts` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year does your disability pension commence to be payable?
      `the Pension Index for 1986 and each later year in order, up to the year it starts` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for 1986, then for each later year in order, up to the year your pension commences?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the flat rate part of my disability pension` IS
    `s 56(2) — the flat rate benefit of a disability pension` `the year my disability pension starts` `the Pension Index for 1986 and each later year in order, up to the year it starts`

-- s 56(3), (4), (4.1). 25% of your average monthly pensionable earnings, which are your total pensionable earnings divided by your months in the contributory period or 48 (24 if you were deemed disabled in 1997), whichever months are greater.
@export What part of my retirement pension from my base earnings counts for my disability pension (s 56(3), (4), (4.1))?
GIVEN `the year I am deemed to have become disabled` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year are you deemed to have become disabled?
      `my total pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total pensionable earnings, in dollars?
      `the months in my contributory period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in your contributory period?
      `the months deducted for child-raising or low earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months were deducted from your contributory period under subsections 48(2) and (4) of the Act?
      `the earnings of the months deducted` IS A NUMBER @desc What pensionable earnings are attributable to those deducted months, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What part of my retirement pension from my base earnings counts for my disability pension` IS
    `s 56(3) — the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension` `the year I am deemed to have become disabled` `my earnings`
    WHERE
        `my earnings` MEANS `cp4 Earnings record for a disability pension` WITH
            `the disabled contributor's total pensionable earnings` IS `my total pensionable earnings`
            `the number of months in the disabled contributor's contributory period` IS `the months in my contributory period`
            `the number of those months deducted under subsections 48(2) and (4)` IS `the months deducted for child-raising or low earnings`
            `the pensionable earnings attributable to the months so deducted` IS `the earnings of the months deducted`

-- s 56(3.1), (4.01). 8.33% of your first additional monthly pensionable earnings: total first additional earnings divided by 480 months, or the 480 highest months divided by 480.
@export What part of my disability pension comes from my first additional earnings (s 56(3.1), (4.01))?
GIVEN `my first additional contributory period, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in your first additional contributory period?
      `my total first additional pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total first additional pensionable earnings, in dollars?
      `the aggregate of my 480 highest first additional months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate of your 480 highest first additional pensionable earnings for a month, in dollars? (Only needed if your first additional contributory period is longer than 480 months)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What part of my disability pension comes from my first additional earnings` IS
    `s 56(3.1) — the first additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension` (`s 56(4.01) — the first additional monthly pensionable earnings` `my first additional contributory period, in months` `my total first additional pensionable earnings` `the aggregate of my 480 highest first additional months`)

-- s 56(3.2), (4.02). 33.33% of your second additional monthly pensionable earnings.
@export What part of my disability pension comes from my second additional earnings (s 56(3.2), (4.02))?
GIVEN `my second additional contributory period, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in your second additional contributory period?
      `my total second additional pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total second additional pensionable earnings, in dollars?
      `the aggregate of my 480 highest second additional months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate of your 480 highest second additional pensionable earnings for a month, in dollars? (Only needed if your second additional contributory period is longer than 480 months)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What part of my disability pension comes from my second additional earnings` IS
    `s 56(3.2) — the second additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension` (`s 56(4.02) — the second additional monthly pensionable earnings` `my second additional contributory period, in months` `my total second additional pensionable earnings` `the aggregate of my 480 highest second additional months`)

-- s 56(1). The disability pension is a flat rate benefit plus 75% of the contributor's retirement pension, the aggregate of the three portions above.
@export How much is my monthly disability pension (s 56(1))?
GIVEN `the year my disability pension starts` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year does your disability pension commence to be payable?
      `the Pension Index for 1986 and each later year in order, up to the year it starts` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for 1986, then for each later year in order, up to the year your pension commences?
      `the year I am deemed to have become disabled` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year are you deemed to have become disabled?
      `my total pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total pensionable earnings, in dollars?
      `the months in my contributory period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in your contributory period?
      `the months deducted for child-raising or low earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months were deducted from your contributory period under subsections 48(2) and (4) of the Act?
      `the earnings of the months deducted` IS A NUMBER @desc What pensionable earnings are attributable to those deducted months, in dollars?
      `my first additional contributory period, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in your first additional contributory period?
      `my total first additional pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total first additional pensionable earnings, in dollars?
      `the aggregate of my 480 highest first additional months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate of your 480 highest first additional pensionable earnings for a month, in dollars? (Only needed if your first additional contributory period is longer than 480 months)
      `my second additional contributory period, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in your second additional contributory period?
      `my total second additional pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total second additional pensionable earnings, in dollars?
      `the aggregate of my 480 highest second additional months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate of your 480 highest second additional pensionable earnings for a month, in dollars? (Only needed if your second additional contributory period is longer than 480 months)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my monthly disability pension` IS
    CONSIDER `s 56(2) — the flat rate benefit of a disability pension` `the year my disability pension starts` `the Pension Index for 1986 and each later year in order, up to the year it starts`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST flat THEN
        CONSIDER `s 56(3) — the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension` `the year I am deemed to have become disabled` `my earnings`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST base THEN JUST (`s 56(1) — the basic monthly amount of a disability pension` flat (`cp4 Retirement pension portions` WITH
            `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension` IS base
            `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `s 56(3.1) — the first additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension` (`s 56(4.01) — the first additional monthly pensionable earnings` `my first additional contributory period, in months` `my total first additional pensionable earnings` `the aggregate of my 480 highest first additional months`)
            `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `s 56(3.2) — the second additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension` (`s 56(4.02) — the second additional monthly pensionable earnings` `my second additional contributory period, in months` `my total second additional pensionable earnings` `the aggregate of my 480 highest second additional months`)))
    WHERE
        `my earnings` MEANS `cp4 Earnings record for a disability pension` WITH
            `the disabled contributor's total pensionable earnings` IS `my total pensionable earnings`
            `the number of months in the disabled contributor's contributory period` IS `the months in my contributory period`
            `the number of those months deducted under subsections 48(2) and (4)` IS `the months deducted for child-raising or low earnings`
            `the pensionable earnings attributable to the months so deducted` IS `the earnings of the months deducted`

-- s 56(6). A division of unadjusted pensionable earnings that reduces your disability pension changes the base portion by weighting the amounts before and after the division.
@export What base portion of my retirement pension counts for my disability pension after a division reduced it (s 56(6))?
GIVEN `the division reduces my disability pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the division reduce the disability pension otherwise payable to you?
      `the portion before the division` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base portion of your retirement pension calculated before the division, in dollars a month?
      `the portion after the division` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base portion calculated following the division, in dollars a month?
      `months excluded for disability` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months were excluded from your contributory period by reason of disability?
      `months until I reach 65` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months remain until the month in which you reach 65?
      `months in my contributory period under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in your contributory period as subsection 56(5) counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What base portion of my retirement pension counts for my disability pension after a division reduced it` IS
    `s 56(6) — the base portion of the retirement pension when a division reduces the disability pension` `the division reduces my disability pension` `the portion before the division` `the portion after the division` `months excluded for disability` `months until I reach 65` `months in my contributory period under the Act`
§§ `Death benefit (section 57) -- apply if a contributor has died`

-- s 57. The death benefit is a lump sum paid to the estate or succession of a contributor who has died.
@export How much death benefit is paid to the estate of the contributor who died (s 57)?
GIVEN `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the contributor die?
      `a retirement pension was payable to the contributor for the month of death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a retirement pension payable to the contributor for the month in which they died?
      `the retirement pension payable for that month` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was the contributor's monthly retirement pension for that month? (0 if none)
      `the contributory period ended before 1976` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the contributor's contributory period end before January 1976?
      `the contributor's basic number of contributory months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contributor's basic number of contributory months (120 less the months excluded by reason of disability)?
      `the months in the contributor's contributory period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months were in the contributor's contributory period?
      `the contributor's total pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the contributor's total pensionable earnings, in dollars?
      `the Pension Index for the year of death` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the year that includes the month in which the contributor died?
      `the Pension Index for the year the pension first became payable` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor's retirement pension first became payable? (Any number if none was payable)
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year of death` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died, in dollars?
      `a death benefit is payable under paragraph 44(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a death benefit payable to the contributor's estate or succession?
      `the contributor received a retirement pension or a disability pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the contributor ever receive a retirement pension or a disability pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan?
      `a survivor's pension is payable because of the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a survivor's pension payable because of the contributor's death?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much death benefit is paid to the estate of the contributor who died` IS
    `s 57(1) — the amount of the death benefit` `the contributor` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year of death` `a death benefit is payable under paragraph 44(1)(c)` `the contributor received a retirement pension or a disability pension` `a survivor's pension is payable because of the death`
    WHERE
        `the contributor` MEANS `cp4 Deceased contributor` WITH
            `cp4 the day the contributor died` IS `the day the contributor died`
            `cp4 a retirement pension was payable to the contributor for the month in which the contributor died` IS `a retirement pension was payable to the contributor for the month of death`
            `cp4 the retirement pension payable to the contributor for the month in which the contributor died` IS `the retirement pension payable for that month`
            `cp4 the contributor's contributory period ended before January 1976` IS `the contributory period ended before 1976`
            `cp4 the contributor's basic number of contributory months` IS `the contributor's basic number of contributory months`
            `cp4 the number of months in the contributor's contributory period` IS `the months in the contributor's contributory period`
            `cp4 the contributor's total pensionable earnings` IS `the contributor's total pensionable earnings`
            `cp4 the Pension Index for the year that includes the month in which the contributor died` IS `the Pension Index for the year of death`
            `cp4 the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor's retirement pension first became payable` IS `the Pension Index for the year the pension first became payable`
§§ `Survivor's pension (section 58) -- ask only if you are the survivor of a contributor who has died`

-- s 58(1.1). The flat rate part of a survivor's pension: $91.06 for 1986, and each later year the previous year's amount times the Pension Index ratio.
@export What is the flat rate part of my survivor's pension (s 58(1.1))?
GIVEN `the year my survivor's pension starts` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year does your survivor's pension commence to be payable?
      `the Pension Index for 1986 and each later year in order, up to the year it starts` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for 1986, then for each later year in order, up to the year your pension commences?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the flat rate part of my survivor's pension` IS
    `s 58(1.1) — the flat rate benefit of a survivor's pension` `the year my survivor's pension starts` `the Pension Index for 1986 and each later year in order, up to the year it starts`

-- s 58(3), (4). The base portion of the contributor's retirement pension used for a survivor's pension, indexed by the Pension Index from the month a listed event occurs.
@export What base portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month (s 58(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the amount calculated under paragraph 57(2)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contributor's retirement pension, as calculated for the death benefit under section 57(2), in dollars a month?
      `the month` IS A DATE @desc For which month is your survivor's pension being calculated (any date in it)?
      `the months in which one of the listed events occurred` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc In which months did one of these happen: your survivor's pension became payable because of a disability that began after the death; you reached 65 (not having reached it at the death); your survivor's pension or your own retirement pension began; your survivor's pension became payable in other circumstances; your retirement pension was adjusted after a division? (A list of dates, one in each month; empty if none)
      `the Pension Index for the year that includes the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the year that includes that month?
      `the year the contributor died` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year did the contributor die?
      `the year my survivor's pension commences` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year does your survivor's pension commence?
      `the Pension Index for the year the contributor died` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor died?
      `the Pension Index for the year the contributor died, without the 1.02 limit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for that year calculated as if it had not been limited to 1.02 times the previous year's? (For a death before 1974; otherwise repeat the number above)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What base portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month` IS
    CONSIDER `cp4 the ratio of one Pension Index value to another` `the Pension Index for the year that includes the month` (`s 58(4) — the Pension Index for the year of the contributor's death that the ratio of subsection (3) uses` `the year the contributor died` `the year my survivor's pension commences` `the Pension Index for the year the contributor died` `the Pension Index for the year the contributor died, without the 1.02 limit`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST ratio THEN JUST (`s 58(3) — the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension` `the amount calculated under paragraph 57(2)(a), (b) or (c)` `the month` `the months in which one of the listed events occurred` ratio)

-- s 58(3.1), (3.2), (3.3). The first additional portion: 8.33% of the first additional monthly pensionable earnings, indexed.
@export What first additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month (s 58(3.1), (3.2))?
GIVEN `a retirement pension was payable to the contributor for the month of death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a retirement pension payable to the contributor for the month in which they died?
      `the contributor's first additional monthly pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the contributor's first additional monthly pensionable earnings, in dollars a month?
      `the Pension Index for the year of the month of death` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the year that includes the month in which the contributor died?
      `the Pension Index for the year the contributor's retirement pension first became payable` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor's retirement pension first became payable? (Any number if none was payable)
      `the month` IS A DATE @desc For which month is your survivor's pension being calculated (any date in it)?
      `the months in which one of the listed events occurred` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc In which months did one of these happen: your survivor's pension became payable because of a disability that began after the death; you reached 65 (not having reached it at the death); your survivor's pension or your own retirement pension began; your survivor's pension became payable in other circumstances; your retirement pension was adjusted after a division? (A list of dates, one in each month; empty if none)
      `the Pension Index for the year that includes the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the year that includes that month?
      `the Pension Index for the year the contributor died` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor died?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What first additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month` IS
    CONSIDER `cp4 the ratio of one Pension Index value to another` `the Pension Index for the year of the month of death` `the Pension Index for the year the contributor's retirement pension first became payable`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST deathRatio THEN
        CONSIDER `cp4 the ratio of one Pension Index value to another` `the Pension Index for the year that includes the month` `the Pension Index for the year the contributor died`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST monthRatio THEN JUST (`s 58(3.1) — the first additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension` (`s 58(3.2) — the amount calculated for the purpose of subsection (3.1)` `a retirement pension was payable to the contributor for the month of death` `the contributor's first additional monthly pensionable earnings` deathRatio) `the month` `the months in which one of the listed events occurred` monthRatio)

-- s 58(3.4), (3.5), (3.6). The second additional portion: 33.33% of the second additional monthly pensionable earnings, indexed.
@export What second additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month (s 58(3.4), (3.5))?
GIVEN `a retirement pension was payable to the contributor for the month of death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a retirement pension payable to the contributor for the month in which they died?
      `the contributor's second additional monthly pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the contributor's second additional monthly pensionable earnings, in dollars a month?
      `the Pension Index for the year of the month of death` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the year that includes the month in which the contributor died?
      `the Pension Index for the year the contributor's retirement pension first became payable` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor's retirement pension first became payable? (Any number if none was payable)
      `the month` IS A DATE @desc For which month is your survivor's pension being calculated (any date in it)?
      `the months in which one of the listed events occurred` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc In which months did one of these happen: your survivor's pension became payable because of a disability that began after the death; you reached 65 (not having reached it at the death); your survivor's pension or your own retirement pension began; your survivor's pension became payable in other circumstances; your retirement pension was adjusted after a division? (A list of dates, one in each month; empty if none)
      `the Pension Index for the year that includes the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the year that includes that month?
      `the Pension Index for the year the contributor died` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor died?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What second additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month` IS
    CONSIDER `cp4 the ratio of one Pension Index value to another` `the Pension Index for the year of the month of death` `the Pension Index for the year the contributor's retirement pension first became payable`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST deathRatio THEN
        CONSIDER `cp4 the ratio of one Pension Index value to another` `the Pension Index for the year that includes the month` `the Pension Index for the year the contributor died`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST monthRatio THEN JUST (`s 58(3.4) — the second additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension` (`s 58(3.5) — the amount calculated for the purpose of subsection (3.4)` `a retirement pension was payable to the contributor for the month of death` `the contributor's second additional monthly pensionable earnings` deathRatio) `the month` `the months in which one of the listed events occurred` monthRatio)

-- s 58(1). The survivor's pension where no retirement pension is payable to the survivor: a flat rate benefit and a share of the contributor's retirement pension, reduced before 2019 for a survivor who was young at the death and neither disabled nor caring for children.
@export How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I get no retirement pension (s 58(1))?
GIVEN `the month` IS A DATE @desc For which month do you want the pension (any date in it)?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I get a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a retirement pension payable to you under the Act or a provincial pension plan?
      `the flat rate part` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the flat rate part of your survivor's pension (section 58(1.1)), in dollars a month?
      `the base portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension used for your pension (section 58(3)), in dollars a month?
      `the first additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional portion (section 58(3.1)), in dollars a month?
      `the second additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional portion (section 58(3.4)), in dollars a month?
      `I had dependent children when the contributor died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you, when the contributor died, a survivor who wholly or substantially maintained one or more dependent children of the contributor?
      `I am disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disabled?
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the contributor die?
      `my circumstances changed after the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, after the death, stop being a survivor with dependent children while not disabled, or stop being disabled while not a survivor with dependent children?
      `the day my circumstances changed` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that happen? (Any date if it did not)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I get no retirement pension` IS
    `s 58(1) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where no retirement pension is payable to the survivor` `the month` `my date of birth` `I get a retirement pension` `the flat rate part` `the portions of the contributor's retirement pension` `I had dependent children when the contributor died` `I am disabled` `the day the contributor died` `the day my circumstances changed, if they did`
    WHERE
        `the portions of the contributor's retirement pension` MEANS `cp4 Retirement pension portions` WITH
            `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension` IS `the base portion`
            `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `the first additional portion`
            `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `the second additional portion`
        `the day my circumstances changed, if they did` MEANS
            IF `my circumstances changed after the death` THEN JUST `the day my circumstances changed` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 58(2), (5). Where a survivor's pension and your own retirement pension are both payable, the two together are capped.
@export How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I also get a retirement pension (s 58(2), (5))?
GIVEN `both a survivor's pension and a retirement pension are payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are both a survivor's pension under the Act and a retirement pension under the Act or a provincial pension plan payable to you?
      `the month` IS A DATE @desc For which month do you want the pension (any date in it)?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day my retirement pension commences` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your retirement pension commence to be payable?
      `the flat rate part` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the flat rate part of your survivor's pension (section 58(1.1)), in dollars a month?
      `a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a post-retirement disability benefit payable to you?
      `my post-retirement disability benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is that benefit, in dollars a month? (0 if none)
      `the contributor's base portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension used for your pension (section 58(3)), in dollars a month?
      `the contributor's first additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional portion (section 58(3.1)), in dollars a month?
      `the contributor's second additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional portion (section 58(3.4)), in dollars a month?
      `my own base portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base portion of your own retirement pension (paragraph 46(1)(a)), without regard to subsections 46(3) to (6) and adjusted under 45(2), in dollars a month?
      `my own first additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional portion of your own retirement pension (paragraph 46(1)(b)), in dollars a month?
      `my own second additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional portion of your own retirement pension (paragraph 46(1)(c)), in dollars a month?
      `my own retirement pension under a provincial plan was reduced because I am over 65 or earn` IS A NUMBER @desc If your retirement pension comes from a provincial plan, how much does that plan take away because you are over 65 or because of your employment earnings, in dollars a month? (0 if none; the Act ignores such reductions)
      `my Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the later of the year you first qualified for the survivor's pension and the year your retirement pension commenced, in dollars?
      `the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that later year and the two years before it, in dollars?
      `the adjustment under subsection 45(2)` IS A NUMBER @desc By what ratio is a benefit adjusted under subsection 45(2) as if it had commenced in that later year? (1 if no adjustment)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I also get a retirement pension` IS
    `s 58(2) — the basic monthly amount of a survivor's pension where a retirement pension is also payable to the survivor` `both a survivor's pension and a retirement pension are payable to me` `the month` `my date of birth` `the day my retirement pension commences` `the flat rate part` `a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to me` `my post-retirement disability benefit` `the contributor's portions` `my own portions` (`cp4 a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of an average, adjusted` `my Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` `the adjustment under subsection 45(2)`) (`cp4 a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of an average, adjusted` `the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the adjustment under subsection 45(2)`)
    WHERE
        `the contributor's portions` MEANS `cp4 Retirement pension portions` WITH
            `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension` IS `the contributor's base portion`
            `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `the contributor's first additional portion`
            `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `the contributor's second additional portion`
        -- Subsection (5): the survivor's own retirement pension is taken without regard to a provincial plan's reduction for those over 65 or earning.
        `my own portions` MEANS `cp4 Retirement pension portions` WITH
            `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension` IS `s 58(5) — the monthly amount of the survivor's retirement pension to use in subsection (2)` `my own base portion` `my own retirement pension under a provincial plan was reduced because I am over 65 or earn`
            `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `my own first additional portion`
            `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `my own second additional portion`

-- s 58(9). A survivor first becomes qualified in the month after the month in which they first met the criteria of subsection 44(1).
@export From which month am I qualified to receive my survivor's pension (s 58(9))?
GIVEN `the month I first met the criteria of subsection 44(1)` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you first meet the criteria of subsection 44(1) for the survivor's pension (any date in it)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From which month am I qualified to receive my survivor's pension` IS
    `s 58(9) — the month in which the survivor first becomes qualified to receive the survivor's pension` `the month I first met the criteria of subsection 44(1)`

-- s 58(6), (6.1), (6.2). Where a survivor's pension and a disability pension are both payable, the disability pension is whatever brings the two up to an aggregate set by the Act.
@export How much is my monthly disability pension where I also get a survivor's pension (s 58(6), (6.1), (6.2))?
GIVEN `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the contributor die?
      `the day I am deemed to have become disabled` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of the Act?
      `the survivor's flat rate benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the flat rate benefit of your survivor's pension (subparagraph 58(1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)), in dollars a month?
      `the disability flat rate benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the flat rate benefit of your disability pension (paragraph 56(1)(a)), in dollars a month?
      `the contributor's base portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension used for your survivor's pension (subsection 58(3)), in dollars a month?
      `the contributor's first additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional portion (subsection 58(3.1)), in dollars a month?
      `the contributor's second additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional portion (subsection 58(3.4)), in dollars a month?
      `my own base portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base portion of the retirement pension that counts for your disability pension (subsection 56(3)), in dollars a month?
      `my own first additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional portion that counts for your disability pension (subsection 56(3.1)), in dollars a month?
      `my own second additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional portion that counts for your disability pension (subsection 56(3.2)), in dollars a month?
      `my Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the later of the year you first qualified for the survivor's pension and the year your disability pension commenced, in dollars?
      `the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that later year and the two years before it, in dollars?
      `the adjustment under subsection 45(2)` IS A NUMBER @desc By what ratio is a benefit adjusted under subsection 45(2) as if it had commenced in that later year? (1 if no adjustment)
      `my survivor's pension` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your survivor's pension for a month in the year in which your survivor's pension or your disability pension commenced, whichever is later, in dollars?
      `the disability pension alone` IS A NUMBER @desc How much would your disability pension be if no survivor's pension were payable, in dollars a month?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my monthly disability pension where I also get a survivor's pension` IS
    `s 58(6), (6.1) and (6.2) — the amount of the disability pension payable with a survivor's pension` `the day the contributor died` `the day I am deemed to have become disabled` `the survivor's flat rate benefit` `the disability flat rate benefit` `the contributor's portions` `my disability portions` (`cp4 a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of an average, adjusted` `my Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` `the adjustment under subsection 45(2)`) (`cp4 a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of an average, adjusted` `the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the adjustment under subsection 45(2)`) `my survivor's pension` `the disability pension alone`
    WHERE
        `the contributor's portions` MEANS `cp4 Retirement pension portions` WITH
            `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension` IS `the contributor's base portion`
            `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `the contributor's first additional portion`
            `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `the contributor's second additional portion`
        `my disability portions` MEANS `cp4 Retirement pension portions` WITH
            `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension` IS `my own base portion`
            `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `my own first additional portion`
            `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `my own second additional portion`

-- s 58(7). The Minister may, on your written request and in prescribed circumstances, pay you the full disability pension and cut the survivor's pension instead.
@export How much is my survivor's pension if the Minister pays me the full disability pension instead (s 58(7))?
GIVEN `the prescribed circumstances exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in the circumstances regulation 54.4 prescribes (financially prejudiced by the survivor's pension but not by the disability pension)?
      `I made a written request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a written request?
      `the Minister is of the opinion that it is to my advantage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it, in the Minister's opinion, to your advantage?
      `the aggregate under subsection (6)` IS A NUMBER @desc What would your survivor's pension and your disability pension add up to under subsection 58(6) (and 58(6.1)), in dollars a month?
      `the full disability pension` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your full disability pension, in dollars a month?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my survivor's pension if the Minister pays me the full disability pension instead` IS
    `s 58(7) — the survivor's pension where the Minister pays the full disability pension` `the prescribed circumstances exist` `I made a written request` `the Minister is of the opinion that it is to my advantage` `the aggregate under subsection (6)` `the full disability pension`

-- s 58(8), (8.1). Where your disability pension is paid under a provincial plan, it is your survivor's pension that is the balance.
@export How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I also get a disability pension under a provincial pension plan (s 58(8), (8.1))?
GIVEN `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the contributor die?
      `the day I am deemed to have become disabled under the provincial plan` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of the provincial pension plan?
      `an agreement under section 80 provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an agreement under section 80 of the Act provide otherwise?
      `the survivor's flat rate benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the flat rate benefit of your survivor's pension (subparagraph 58(1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)), in dollars a month?
      `the provincial plan's flat rate benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the flat rate benefit payable under the provincial plan in respect of disability, in dollars a month?
      `the contributor's base portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension used for your survivor's pension (subsection 58(3)), in dollars a month?
      `the contributor's first additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional portion (subsection 58(3.1)), in dollars a month?
      `the contributor's second additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional portion (subsection 58(3.4)), in dollars a month?
      `the provincial base portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension payable to you under the provincial plan in respect of disability, in dollars a month?
      `the provincial first additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional portion payable under the provincial plan, in dollars a month?
      `the provincial second additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional portion payable under the provincial plan, in dollars a month?
      `my Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the later of the year you first qualified for the survivor's pension and the year your disability pension commenced, in dollars?
      `the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that later year and the two years before it, in dollars?
      `the adjustment under subsection 45(2)` IS A NUMBER @desc By what ratio is a benefit adjusted under subsection 45(2) as if it had commenced in that later year? (1 if no adjustment)
      `my disability pension under the provincial plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your disability pension under the provincial plan for a month in the year in which your survivor's pension or that disability pension commenced, whichever is later, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I also get a disability pension under a provincial pension plan` IS
    IF `s 58(8) — subsection (8) applies` `the day the contributor died` `the day I am deemed to have become disabled under the provincial plan` `an agreement under section 80 provides otherwise`
    THEN JUST (`s 58(8) — the amount of the survivor's pension where a disability pension is also payable under a provincial pension plan` `the survivor's flat rate benefit` `the provincial plan's flat rate benefit` `the contributor's portions` `the provincial portions` (`cp4 a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of an average, adjusted` `my Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` `the adjustment under subsection 45(2)`) `my disability pension under the provincial plan`)
    ELSE
        -- Subsection (8.1) is the rule where (8) does not apply "except where otherwise provided by an agreement under section 80".
        IF `an agreement under section 80 provides otherwise`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (`s 58(8.1) — the amount of the survivor's pension where a disability pension is also payable under a provincial pension plan and subsection (8) does not apply` `the survivor's flat rate benefit` `the provincial plan's flat rate benefit` `the contributor's portions` `the provincial portions` (`cp4 a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of an average, adjusted` `the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the adjustment under subsection 45(2)`) `my disability pension under the provincial plan`)
    WHERE
        `the contributor's portions` MEANS `cp4 Retirement pension portions` WITH
            `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension` IS `the contributor's base portion`
            `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `the contributor's first additional portion`
            `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `the contributor's second additional portion`
        `the provincial portions` MEANS `cp4 Retirement pension portions` WITH
            `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension` IS `the provincial base portion`
            `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `the provincial first additional portion`
            `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `the provincial second additional portion`
§§ `Disabled contributor's child's benefit and orphan's benefit (section 59) -- ask only if you are the child of a disabled contributor, or an orphan, or look after one`

-- s 59. The benefit is $113.14 a month in 1991 and is indexed every year (with $35 added in 1992); a dependent child in part-time attendance at school or university gets half.
@export How much is the monthly benefit for a child of a disabled contributor, or for an orphan (s 59)?
GIVEN `the child is in part-time attendance at a school or university` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the dependent child aged 18 or over but under 25 and in part-time attendance at a school or university?
      `the year the benefit starts` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year does the benefit commence to be payable?
      `the Pension Index for 1986 and each later year in order, up to the year it starts` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for 1986, then for each later year in order, up to the year the benefit commences?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the monthly benefit for a child of a disabled contributor, or for an orphan` IS
    `s 59 — the basic monthly amount of the benefit for the child` `the child is in part-time attendance at a school or university` `the year the benefit starts` `the Pension Index for 1986 and each later year in order, up to the year it starts`

§§ `Post-retirement benefit and post-retirement disability benefit (sections 59.1 and 59.2) -- ask only if you are getting a retirement pension and still working and contributing`

-- s 59.1(1.1), (2), (7). The base portion of the post-retirement benefit.
@export What is the base portion of my monthly post-retirement benefit (s 59.1(1.1), (2), (7))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the first day of the year my post-retirement benefit starts` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the year in which your post-retirement benefit commences to be payable?
      `the adjustment factor for my age that day` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the adjustment factor (subsection 46(3) or (3.1)) for your age on that day?
      `the adjustment factor for age 70` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the adjustment factor for a contributor who is 70?
      `my earnings are earned in the year my contributory period ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your base unadjusted pensionable earnings earned in the year in which your contributory period ends?
      `my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year before` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount determined under subsection 53(1) for the year before the year your post-retirement benefit commences, in dollars?
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year my contributory period ends` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which your contributory period ends, in dollars?
      `the months in the year before my retirement pension becomes payable` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in the year before your retirement pension becomes payable?
      `the earnings of subparagraph 53(1)(b)(i)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the earnings referred to in subparagraph 53(1)(b)(i), in dollars?
      `the aggregate of the earnings of subparagraphs 53(1)(b)(i) and (ii)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate of the earnings in subparagraphs 53(1)(b)(i) and (ii), in dollars?
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year before` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year before the year your post-retirement benefit commences, in dollars?
      `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year my benefit starts` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year your post-retirement benefit commences, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the base portion of my monthly post-retirement benefit` IS
    `s 59.1(1.1) — the base portion of a post-retirement benefit` (`s 59.1(2) — the amount used for A in subsection (1.1)` `my earnings are earned in the year my contributory period ends` `my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year before` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year my contributory period ends` `the months in the year before my retirement pension becomes payable`) `the earnings of subparagraph 53(1)(b)(i)` `the aggregate of the earnings of subparagraphs 53(1)(b)(i) and (ii)` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year before` `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year my benefit starts` (`s 59.1(7) — the adjustment factor E` `my date of birth` `the first day of the year my post-retirement benefit starts` `the adjustment factor for my age that day` `the adjustment factor for age 70`)

-- s 59.1(3), (4), (7). The first additional portion of the post-retirement benefit.
@export What is the first additional portion of my monthly post-retirement benefit (s 59.1(3), (4), (7))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the first day of the year my post-retirement benefit starts` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the year in which your post-retirement benefit commences to be payable?
      `the year my post-retirement benefit starts` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year does your post-retirement benefit commence?
      `the adjustment factor for my age that day` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the adjustment factor (subsection 46(3.1)) for your age on that day?
      `the adjustment factor for age 70` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the adjustment factor for a contributor who is 70?
      `my earnings are earned in the year my first additional contributory period ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings earned in the year in which your first additional contributory period ends?
      `my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year before` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount determined under subsection 53.1(1) for the year before the year your post-retirement benefit commences, in dollars?
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year my first additional period ends` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which your first additional contributory period ends, in dollars?
      `the months in the year before my retirement pension becomes payable` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in the year before your retirement pension becomes payable?
      `the earnings of subparagraph 53.1(1)(b)(i)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the earnings referred to in subparagraph 53.1(1)(b)(i), in dollars?
      `the aggregate of the earnings of subparagraphs 53.1(1)(b)(i) and (ii)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate of the earnings in subparagraphs 53.1(1)(b)(i) and (ii), in dollars?
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year before` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year before the year your post-retirement benefit commences, in dollars?
      `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year my benefit starts` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year your post-retirement benefit commences, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the first additional portion of my monthly post-retirement benefit` IS
    `s 59.1(3) — the first additional portion of a post-retirement benefit` (`s 59.1(4) — the amount used for A in subsection (3)` `my earnings are earned in the year my first additional contributory period ends` (`s 59.1(3) — the amount A used in subsection (3) before subsection (4)` `the year my post-retirement benefit starts` `my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year before`) `my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year before` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year my first additional period ends` `the months in the year before my retirement pension becomes payable`) `the earnings of subparagraph 53.1(1)(b)(i)` `the aggregate of the earnings of subparagraphs 53.1(1)(b)(i) and (ii)` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year before` `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year my benefit starts` (`s 59.1(7) — the adjustment factor E` `my date of birth` `the first day of the year my post-retirement benefit starts` `the adjustment factor for my age that day` `the adjustment factor for age 70`)

-- s 59.1(5), (6), (7). The second additional portion of the post-retirement benefit.
@export What is the second additional portion of my monthly post-retirement benefit (s 59.1(5), (6), (7))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the first day of the year my post-retirement benefit starts` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the year in which your post-retirement benefit commences to be payable?
      `the adjustment factor for my age that day` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the adjustment factor (subsection 46(3.1)) for your age on that day?
      `the adjustment factor for age 70` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the adjustment factor for a contributor who is 70?
      `my earnings are earned in the year my second additional contributory period ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings earned in the year in which your second additional contributory period ends?
      `my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year before` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount determined under section 53.2 for the year before the year your post-retirement benefit commences, in dollars?
      `the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year my second additional period ends` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which your second additional contributory period ends, in dollars?
      `the months in the year before my retirement pension becomes payable` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in the year before your retirement pension becomes payable?
      `the earnings of subparagraph 53.2(1)(b)(i)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the earnings referred to in subparagraph 53.2(1)(b)(i), in dollars?
      `the aggregate of the earnings of subparagraphs 53.2(1)(b)(i) and (ii)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate of the earnings in subparagraphs 53.2(1)(b)(i) and (ii), in dollars?
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year before` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year before the year your post-retirement benefit commences, in dollars?
      `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year my benefit starts` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year your post-retirement benefit commences, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the second additional portion of my monthly post-retirement benefit` IS
    `s 59.1(5) — the second additional portion of a post-retirement benefit` (`s 59.1(6) — the amount used for A in subsection (5)` `my earnings are earned in the year my second additional contributory period ends` `my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year before` `the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year my second additional period ends` `the months in the year before my retirement pension becomes payable`) `the earnings of subparagraph 53.2(1)(b)(i)` `the aggregate of the earnings of subparagraphs 53.2(1)(b)(i) and (ii)` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year before` `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year my benefit starts` (`s 59.1(7) — the adjustment factor E` `my date of birth` `the first day of the year my post-retirement benefit starts` `the adjustment factor for my age that day` `the adjustment factor for age 70`)

-- s 59.1(1). The post-retirement benefit is the aggregate of the three portions.
@export How much is my monthly post-retirement benefit in all (s 59.1(1))?
GIVEN `the base portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base portion of your post-retirement benefit, in dollars a month?
      `the first additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional portion, in dollars a month?
      `the second additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional portion, in dollars a month?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my monthly post-retirement benefit in all` IS
    `s 59.1(1) — the basic monthly amount of a post-retirement benefit` (JUST `the base portion`) (JUST `the first additional portion`) (JUST `the second additional portion`)

-- s 59.2. The post-retirement disability benefit is $485.20 times the Pension Index ratio in 2019 and indexed every year after.
@export How much is my monthly post-retirement disability benefit (s 59.2)?
GIVEN `the year the benefit is payable` IS A NUMBER @desc For which year do you want the benefit?
      `the Pension Index for 1986 and each later year in order, up to that year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for 1986, then for each later year in order, up to that year?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my monthly post-retirement disability benefit` IS
    `s 59.2 — the basic monthly amount of a post-retirement disability benefit` `the year the benefit is payable` `the Pension Index for 1986 and each later year in order, up to that year`
§§ `Applying for a benefit (section 60)`

-- s 60(1). No benefit is payable unless an application has been made by you or for you and payment has been approved.
@export Is a benefit payable to me (s 60(1))?
GIVEN `an application has been made by me or for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for the benefit been made by you or on your behalf (including one the Act treats as made)?
      `payment has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has payment of the benefit been approved under the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a benefit payable to me` IS
    `s 60(1) — a benefit is payable to the person` `an application has been made by me or for me` `payment has been approved`

-- s 60(1.1). Your application for a post-retirement benefit is treated as made on 1 January of the year after the earnings.
@export On what day is my application for a post-retirement benefit treated as made (s 60(1.1))?
GIVEN `the year of the earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc For which year are the unadjusted pensionable earnings referred to in section 76.1?
      `I am a beneficiary of a retirement pension on 1 January of the next year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you be a beneficiary of a retirement pension on 1 January of the year after that year?
      `the Minister has the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister have the information necessary to determine whether a post-retirement benefit is payable to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my application for a post-retirement benefit treated as made` IS
    `s 60(1.1) — the day an application for a post-retirement benefit is deemed to be made` `the year of the earnings` `I am a beneficiary of a retirement pension on 1 January of the next year` `the Minister has the information`

-- s 60(1.2), (1.3). The Minister may waive your application for a retirement pension if you are a contributor of 70 or over and receive a benefit or a return of income was filed; the application is then treated as made on the day of the waiver.
@export May the Minister waive my application for a retirement pension (s 60(1.2))?
GIVEN `I am a contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a contributor?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day the Minister considers waiving` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the Minister consider waiving the requirement?
      `I receive a benefit under the Act, the Old Age Security Act or a provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive a benefit under the Canada Pension Plan, the Old Age Security Act or a provincial pension plan?
      `a tax return was filed for the year before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a return of income filed by you or on your behalf for the year before that day's year?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister waive my application for a retirement pension` IS
    `s 60(1.2) — the Minister may waive the requirement for an application for a retirement pension` `I am a contributor` `my date of birth` `the day the Minister considers waiving` `I receive a benefit under the Act, the Old Age Security Act or a provincial plan` `a tax return was filed for the year before`

@export On what day is my application for a retirement pension treated as made if the Minister waives it (s 60(1.3))?
GIVEN `the requirement has been waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister waived the requirement for an application for a retirement pension?
      `the day it was waived` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the requirement waived?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my application for a retirement pension treated as made if the Minister waives it` IS
    `s 60(1.3) — the day the application for a retirement pension is deemed to have been made and received` `the requirement has been waived` `the day it was waived`

-- s 60(2), (2.1), (2.2). The estate, representative or heir of a person who died may apply, within 12 months after the death, for the benefit the person would have received.
@export May the application for a benefit of a person who has died be approved for this month (s 60(2), (2.1), (2.2))?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A `Kind of benefit` @desc Which benefit: a retirement pension, a disability pension, a death benefit, a survivor's pension, a disabled contributor's child's benefit, an orphan's benefit, a post-retirement benefit or a post-retirement disability benefit?
      `the person would have been entitled for the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the person who died, before dying, have been entitled on approval of an application to payment of the benefit for that month?
      `the day the person died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the person die?
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the application made?
      `the day the application is received` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the application received?
      `the applicant is the estate, a representative, an heir or a prescribed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made by the estate, the representative or heir of the person, or by a person prescribed by regulation?
      `the deceased contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What was the contributor's date of birth?
      `the month` IS A DATE @desc For which month is approval in question (any date in it)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the application for a benefit of a person who has died be approved for this month` IS
    `s 60(2) to (2.2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved for the month` `the benefit` `the person would have been entitled for the month` `the day the person died` `the day the application is made` `the day the application is received` `the applicant is the estate, a representative, an heir or a prescribed person` `the deceased contributor's date of birth` `the month`

-- s 60(3). A person with decision-making responsibility may apply within a year after the death of a child or orphan who died before applying.
@export May an application be made for a child's or orphan's benefit after the child or orphan has died (s 60(3))?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A `Kind of benefit` @desc Which benefit: a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit (or another)?
      `it would have been payable on an application made before the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the benefit have been payable to the child or orphan on an application made before the death?
      `the day the child or orphan died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the child or orphan die?
      `the child's or orphan's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What was the child's or orphan's date of birth?
      `no application had been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had no application been made by the time of the death?
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the application made?
      `I have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan at the time of the death?
      `nobody had decision-making responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there at that time no person or agency with decision-making responsibility?
      `the Minister has directed me to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister directed you or your agency to apply?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May an application be made for a child's or orphan's benefit after the child or orphan has died` IS
    `s 60(3) — an application may be made after the death of a child or orphan` `the benefit` `it would have been payable on an application made before the death` `the day the child or orphan died` `the child's or orphan's date of birth` `no application had been made` `the day the application is made` `I have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan` `nobody had decision-making responsibility` `the Minister has directed me to apply`

-- s 60(4). A benefit applied for after a death is paid to the estate or to a person prescribed by regulation.
@export May the benefit applied for after a death be paid to me as payee (s 60(4))?
GIVEN `I am the estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the estate of the person, child or orphan who died?
      `I am a person prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person prescribed by regulation to be paid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the benefit applied for after a death be paid to me as payee` IS
    `s 60(4) — the benefit applied for under subsection (2) or (3) is paid to the payee` `I am the estate` `I am a person prescribed by regulation`

-- s 60(5). Such an application is treated as received on the day of the death.
@export On what day is an application made after a death treated as received (s 60(5))?
GIVEN `the application is made for the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made under subsection (2), for a person who died after being entitled to a benefit?
      `the application is made for a child or orphan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made under subsection (3), for a child or orphan who died?
      `nobody applied before the child or orphan died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person or agency with decision-making responsibility not apply before the child's or orphan's death?
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the person, child or orphan die?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is an application made after a death treated as received` IS
    `s 60(5) — the day an application made under subsection (2) or (3) is deemed to have been received` `the application is made for the person who died` `the application is made for a child or orphan` `nobody applied before the child or orphan died` `the day of the death`

-- s 60(6). An application is made to the Minister in the prescribed manner and at the prescribed location.
@export Is my application for a benefit made as the Act requires (s 60(6))?
GIVEN `made to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made to the Minister?
      `made in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made in the prescribed manner (in writing)?
      `made at the prescribed location` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made at the prescribed location?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my application for a benefit made as the Act requires` IS
    `s 60(6) — an application for a benefit is made as the Act requires` `made to the Minister` `made in the prescribed manner` `made at the prescribed location`

-- s 60(7). The Minister must consider the application at once and notify you in writing of the decision.
@export Must the Minister consider my application at once and tell me the decision in writing (s 60(7))?
GIVEN `the Minister has received my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister received your application for a benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister consider my application at once and tell me the decision in writing` IS
    `s 60(7) — the Minister must consider the application at once and notify the applicant in writing of the decision` `the Minister has received my application`

-- s 60(8), (10), (11). If an application was made for you while you were incapable of making one, the Minister may treat it as made in the month before the first month the benefit could have started, or the month your incapacity began, whichever is later.
@export In which month can the Minister treat an application made for me as made because I was incapable (s 60(8), (10), (11))?
GIVEN `the last day I was incapacitated` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day on which you were incapacitated? (This covers only people incapacitated on or after 1 January 1991.)
      `my incapacity was one continuous period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your period of incapacity one continuous period?
      `a regulation allows an interrupted period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a regulation allow a period of incapacity that was not continuous?
      `the application was made on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the application made on your behalf?
      `the Minister is satisfied I was incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied, on evidence provided by or for you, that you were incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application on your own behalf on the day it was actually made?
      `the first month the benefit could have started` IS A DATE @desc In which month could the benefit first have commenced to be paid (any date in it)?
      `the month my last period of incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the Minister consider your last relevant period of incapacity to have begun (any date in it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `In which month can the Minister treat an application made for me as made because I was incapable` IS
    `s 60(8) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made on behalf of the person to have been made` `the last day I was incapacitated` `my incapacity was one continuous period` `a regulation allows an interrupted period` `the application was made on my behalf` `the Minister is satisfied I was incapable` `the first month the benefit could have started` `the month my last period of incapacity began`

-- s 60(9), (10), (11). If you were incapable before the day you applied but had stopped being incapable, and you applied within the window, the Minister may treat the application as made earlier.
@export In which month can the Minister treat my application as made because I was incapable until shortly before I applied (s 60(9), (10), (11))?
GIVEN `the last day I was incapacitated` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day on which you were incapacitated? (This covers only people incapacitated on or after 1 January 1991.)
      `my incapacity was one continuous period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your period of incapacity one continuous period?
      `a regulation allows an interrupted period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a regulation allow a period of incapacity that was not continuous?
      `the Minister is satisfied I was incapable earlier and had stopped before I applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied, on evidence provided by or for you, that you were incapable of forming or expressing an intention to apply before the day you applied, and had stopped being incapable before that day?
      `the day I stopped being incapable` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you stop being incapable?
      `the days of my incapacity` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days did your period of incapacity last?
      `the day I actually applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your application actually made?
      `the first month the benefit could have started` IS A DATE @desc In which month could the benefit first have commenced to be paid (any date in it)?
      `the month my last period of incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the Minister consider your last relevant period of incapacity to have begun (any date in it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `In which month can the Minister treat my application as made because I was incapable until shortly before I applied` IS
    `s 60(9) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made by or on behalf of the person after incapacity has ceased to have been made` `the last day I was incapacitated` `my incapacity was one continuous period` `a regulation allows an interrupted period` `the Minister is satisfied I was incapable earlier and had stopped before I applied` `the day I stopped being incapable` `the days of my incapacity` `the day I actually applied` `the first month the benefit could have started` `the month my last period of incapacity began`

-- s 60(11.1). Where a disability application is treated as made earlier, the Minister may treat the application for the contributor's child's benefit as made in the same month.
@export Can the Minister treat the application for my child's benefit as made in the same earlier month as my disability application (s 60(11.1))?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A `Kind of benefit` @desc Which benefit was the earlier-deemed application for: a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit (or another)?
      `my application was treated as made in an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your application treated, under subsection (8) or (9), as made in a month before the one in which it was actually made?
      `the month it is treated as made` IS A DATE @desc In which month is it treated as made (any date in it)?
      `the month it was actually made` IS A DATE @desc In which month was it actually made (any date in it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Can the Minister treat the application for my child's benefit as made in the same earlier month as my disability application` IS
    `s 60(11.1) — the month in which the Minister may also deem the application for a disabled contributor's child's benefit to have been made` `the benefit` `the deemed month, if any` `the month it was actually made`
    WHERE
        `the deemed month, if any` MEANS IF `my application was treated as made in an earlier month` THEN JUST `the month it is treated as made` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 60(12). The Minister may require you to be at a suitable place at a suitable time to apply in person or give more information.
@export Must I be at the place and time the Minister requires to apply in person or give information (s 60(12))?
GIVEN `the Minister requires me or a group I am in to be at a suitable place and time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister required you, or a group or class of persons you are in, to be at a suitable place at a suitable time?
      `it is to apply in person or give more information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in order to make an application for benefits in person or to provide additional information about an application?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be at the place and time the Minister requires to apply in person or give information` IS
    `s 60(12) — the person must be at the place and time the Minister requires` `the Minister requires me or a group I am in to be at a suitable place and time` `it is to apply in person or give more information`

§§ `Interim benefit (section 61) -- ask only if your benefit cannot yet be finally calculated`

-- s 61(1). The Minister may approve an interim benefit where the amount cannot yet be fixed.
@export May the Minister approve an interim benefit for me (s 61(1))?
GIVEN `I have applied for a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for a benefit?
      `payment would be approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would payment of the benefit be approved?
      `the amount cannot yet be finally calculated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it that the amount of the benefit cannot be finally calculated at the time approval would otherwise be given?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister approve an interim benefit for me` IS
    `s 61(1) — the Minister may approve payment of an interim benefit` `I have applied for a benefit` `payment would be approved` `the amount cannot yet be finally calculated`

-- s 61(2). When the benefit is approved, the difference is paid to you if the interim benefit was less, or deducted or recovered if it was more.
@export How much more am I paid once my benefit is approved than my interim benefit (s 61(2)(a))?
GIVEN `my interim benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was the interim benefit, in dollars?
      `my approved benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the benefit subsequently approved, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much more am I paid once my benefit is approved than my interim benefit` IS
    `s 61(2)(a) — the additional amount the beneficiary is paid` `my interim benefit` `my approved benefit`

@export How much of my interim benefit must be deducted or recovered once my benefit is approved (s 61(2)(b))?
GIVEN `my interim benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was the interim benefit, in dollars?
      `my approved benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the benefit subsequently approved, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my interim benefit must be deducted or recovered once my benefit is approved` IS
    `s 61(2)(b) — the excess that is deducted from subsequent payments or otherwise recovered` `my interim benefit` `my approved benefit`

§§ `When payment is made (section 62)`

-- s 62(1). Payment is made at the time the Minister directs each month; if approval comes after the first month payable, monthly payments start the month after approval and earlier months are paid in one sum.
@export From which month are my monthly payments made (s 62(1))?
GIVEN `the month the first payment is payable for` IS A DATE @desc For which month is the first payment of the benefit payable (any date in it)?
      `the month payment is approved` IS A DATE @desc In which month is payment of the benefit approved (any date in it)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From which month are my monthly payments made` IS
    `s 62(1) — the month from which monthly payments are made` `the month the first payment is payable for` `the month payment is approved`

@export For how many months am I paid in one sum (s 62(1))?
GIVEN `the month the first payment is payable for` IS A DATE @desc For which month is the first payment of the benefit payable (any date in it)?
      `the month payment is approved` IS A DATE @desc In which month is payment of the benefit approved (any date in it)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many months am I paid in one sum` IS
    `s 62(1) — the number of months for which payment is made in one sum` `the month the first payment is payable for` `the month payment is approved`

-- s 62(2). A benefit payable from a month is deemed payable from the beginning of that month.
@export From which day is my benefit deemed to have become payable (s 62(2))?
GIVEN `the month my benefit is payable from` IS A DATE @desc From which month is your benefit payable (any date in it)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From which day is my benefit deemed to have become payable` IS
    `s 62(2) — the day a benefit is deemed to have become payable` `the month my benefit is payable from`
§§ `Remarriage and the survivor's pension (sections 63 and 63.1) -- ask only if you are a survivor who has remarried, or whose later marriage has ended, or whose survivor's pension is in question`

-- The text of section 63.1 gives no date for "the coming into force of this section": the questions below ask for it.
-- s 63.1(1), 63(1). A remarriage after section 63.1 came into force does not stop a survivor's pension; an earlier one did.
@export Is no survivor's pension payable to me while I am remarried (s 63(1), 63.1(1))?
GIVEN `my spouse has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your spouse died (the spouse who made you a survivor)?
      `I remarried when no survivor's pension was payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you remarry at a time when no survivor's pension was payable to you?
      `I am within the period of the remarriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, on the day in question, within the period of that remarriage?
      `the day I remarried` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you remarry?
      `the day section 63.1 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what date did section 63.1 of the Act come into force? (The text of the Act does not say; enter the date from the amending legislation.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is no survivor's pension payable to me while I am remarried` IS
    `s 63(1) — no survivor's pension is payable to the person on the day` `my spouse has died` `I remarried when no survivor's pension was payable to me` `I am within the period of the remarriage` `the day I remarried` `the day section 63.1 came into force`

@export Is my first deceased spouse treated as the spouse named in my application for a survivor's pension after a later death (s 63(1))?
GIVEN `I remarried when no survivor's pension was payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you remarry at a time when no survivor's pension was payable to you?
      `a survivor's pension would be payable if I applied after the death of that or a later spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a survivor's pension be payable to you if you applied, following the death of the spouse of that remarriage or of any later one?
      `the day I remarried` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you remarry?
      `the day section 63.1 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what date did section 63.1 of the Act come into force? (The text of the Act does not say; enter the date from the amending legislation.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my first deceased spouse treated as the spouse named in my application for a survivor's pension after a later death` IS
    `s 63(1) — the first deceased spouse is deemed to be the spouse named in the application` `I remarried when no survivor's pension was payable to me` `a survivor's pension would be payable if I applied after the death of that or a later spouse` `the day I remarried` `the day section 63.1 came into force`

-- s 63(2). A survivor's pension being paid is discontinued from the month after the month of a remarriage (before section 63.1 came into force).
@export From which month is my survivor's pension discontinued because I remarried (s 63(2))?
GIVEN `a survivor's pension is being paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a survivor's pension being paid to you?
      `the day I married` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you marry?
      `the day section 63.1 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what date did section 63.1 of the Act come into force? (The text of the Act does not say; enter the date from the amending legislation.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which month is my survivor's pension discontinued because I remarried` IS
    `s 63(2) — the month from which the survivor's pension is discontinued` `a survivor's pension is being paid to me` `the day I married` `the day section 63.1 came into force`

-- s 63(3), (8). If your new spouse dies, you may apply to be paid the greater of the pension discontinued and the one the new death gives, but only if the application was pending when section 63.1 came into force.
@export What survivor's pension am I paid on application if my new spouse dies (s 63(3), (8))?
GIVEN `my application under subsection (3) was pending when section 63.1 came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an application under subsection 63(3) that was pending when section 63.1 came into force?
      `my survivor's pension was discontinued and my new spouse has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your survivor's pension discontinued on your remarriage, and has your new spouse died?
      `the survivor's pension that was discontinued` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was the survivor's pension that was discontinued, in dollars a month?
      `the pension the new death would give` IS A NUMBER @desc How much survivor's pension would be payable by reason of the new spouse's death if none had been payable before, in dollars a month?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What survivor's pension am I paid on application if my new spouse dies` IS
    `s 63(3) — the survivor's pension payable to the person on application` `my application under subsection (3) was pending when section 63.1 came into force` `my survivor's pension was discontinued and my new spouse has died` `the survivor's pension that was discontinued` `the pension the new death would give`

-- s 63(4), (9). If the later marriage ends otherwise than by death, the discontinued pension becomes payable again, for a marriage that ended before section 63.1 came into force.
@export Does my discontinued survivor's pension become payable again when my later marriage ends (s 63(4), (9))?
GIVEN `my survivor's pension was discontinued because I remarried` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your survivor's pension discontinued under subsection 63(2) because you remarried?
      `my marriage ended otherwise than by my spouse's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the marriage end otherwise than by the death of your spouse?
      `the day my marriage ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the marriage end?
      `the day section 63.1 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what date did section 63.1 of the Act come into force? (The text of the Act does not say; enter the date from the amending legislation.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my discontinued survivor's pension become payable again when my later marriage ends` IS
    `s 63(4) — the survivor's pension previously payable becomes payable to the person again` `my survivor's pension was discontinued because I remarried` `my marriage ended otherwise than by my spouse's death` `the day my marriage ended` `the day section 63.1 came into force`

-- s 63(5), (10). A pension that again becomes payable is calculated as though it had never been discontinued, except a pension payable under section 63.1.
@export Is my basic monthly amount calculated as though my survivor's pension had never been discontinued (s 63(5), (10))?
GIVEN `my survivor's pension was discontinued because I remarried` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your survivor's pension discontinued under subsection 63(2) because you remarried?
      `the same pension again becomes payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a survivor's pension equal to the one discontinued become payable to you, or has the discontinued one again become payable?
      `it becomes payable under section 63.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the pension become payable to you under section 63.1?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my basic monthly amount calculated as though my survivor's pension had never been discontinued` IS
    `s 63(5) — the basic monthly amount is calculated as though the pension had not been discontinued` `my survivor's pension was discontinued because I remarried` `the same pension again becomes payable` `it becomes payable under section 63.1`

-- s 63(6). Only one survivor's pension is payable: the greatest of those that would be.
@export Which one survivor's pension am I paid if more than one would be payable (s 63(6))?
GIVEN `the survivor's pensions that would be payable at once` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What are the amounts of each survivor's pension that would be payable to you at the same time under the Canada Pension Plan and a provincial pension plan, in dollars a month?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Which one survivor's pension am I paid if more than one would be payable` IS
    `s 63(6) — the one survivor's pension payable to the person` `the survivor's pensions that would be payable at once`

-- s 63(7), (7.1). No survivor's pension is payable if the contributor died within a year of the marriage and the Minister is not satisfied about their health, unless you lived together for a year or more in all.
@export Is my survivor's pension withheld because the contributor died within a year of our marriage (s 63(7), (7.1))?
GIVEN `the day we married` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you marry the contributor?
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the contributor die?
      `the Minister is satisfied about the contributor's health at the marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the contributor was, at the time of the marriage, in such a condition of health as to justify an expectation of surviving for at least one year?
      `days we lived together during the marriage` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days did you live together during the marriage?
      `days we lived together in a conjugal relationship just before the marriage` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days did you live together in a conjugal relationship immediately before the marriage?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my survivor's pension withheld because the contributor died within a year of our marriage` IS
    `s 63(7) — no survivor's pension is payable because the contributor died within a year of the marriage` `the day we married` `the day the contributor died` `the Minister is satisfied about the contributor's health at the marriage` `days we lived together during the marriage` `days we lived together in a conjugal relationship just before the marriage`

-- s 63.1(2). A survivor who lost a pension to section 63(1) or (2) before section 63.1 came into force and is not now being paid may apply in writing for it to be commenced or reinstated.
@export May I apply in writing for my survivor's pension to be commenced or reinstated (s 63.1(2))?
GIVEN `my pension did not become payable because of section 63(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before section 63.1 came into force, did a survivor's pension that would have become payable to you fail to become payable only because of subsection 63(1)?
      `my pension was discontinued under section 63(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before section 63.1 came into force, was payment of a survivor's pension to you discontinued under subsection 63(2)?
      `I am not being paid a survivor's pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not being paid a survivor's pension at the time section 63.1 comes into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply in writing for my survivor's pension to be commenced or reinstated` IS
    `s 63.1(2) — the person may apply in writing to the Minister for the commencement or reinstatement of the survivor's pension` `my pension did not become payable because of section 63(1)` `my pension was discontinued under section 63(2)` `I am not being paid a survivor's pension`

-- s 63.1(3). On approval the pension is payable from the later of the month section 63.1 came into force and the eleventh month before the application was received.
@export From which month is my survivor's pension payable once my application is approved (s 63.1(3))?
GIVEN `the day section 63.1 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what date did section 63.1 of the Act come into force? (The text of the Act does not say; enter the date from the amending legislation.)
      `the day the Minister received my application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Minister receive your application?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From which month is my survivor's pension payable once my application is approved` IS
    `s 63.1(3) — the first month for which the survivor's pension is payable on approval` `the day section 63.1 came into force` `the day the Minister received my application`

-- s 63.1(4). The basic monthly amount is worked out under section 58 from the time it would have become payable, or as though it had never been discontinued.
@export From what time is my basic monthly amount worked out under section 58 (s 63.1(4))?
GIVEN `my pension did not become payable because of section 63(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a survivor's pension that would have become payable to you fail to become payable because of subsection 63(1)? (No, if it was instead discontinued under 63(2))
      `the time it would have become payable` IS A DATE @desc When would the pension have become payable but for subsection 63(1)? (Any date if not applicable)
      `the month it had commenced` IS A DATE @desc With which month had payment of the discontinued pension commenced? (Any date if not applicable)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what time is my basic monthly amount worked out under section 58` IS
    `s 63.1(4) — the time from which the basic monthly amount is calculated in accordance with section 58` `my pension did not become payable because of section 63(1)` `the time it would have become payable` `the month it had commenced`

§§ `Protection of a benefit (section 65) -- ask if someone has tried to take, charge or seize your benefit, or an authority wants to be repaid out of it`

-- s 65(1). A transaction that assigns, charges, attaches, anticipates or gives a benefit as security is void.
@export Is a dealing with my benefit void (s 65(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of dealing` IS A `cp4 Transaction in a benefit` @desc What kind of dealing is it: an assignment, a charge, an attachment, an anticipation, a giving as security, or another transaction?
      `it is an assignment of part of a retirement pension the Minister approved under section 65.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an assignment of a portion of a retirement pension that the Minister has approved under section 65.1?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a dealing with my benefit void` IS
    `s 65(1) — the transaction is void` `the kind of dealing` `it is an assignment of part of a retirement pension the Minister approved under section 65.1`

-- s 65(1.1). A benefit is exempt from seizure and execution.
@export Is my benefit exempt from seizure and execution (s 65(1.1))?
GIVEN `what is being seized is a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what is being seized or executed against a benefit under the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my benefit exempt from seizure and execution` IS
    `s 65(1.1) — the benefit is exempt from seizure and execution` `what is being seized is a benefit`

-- s 65(2). The Minister may deduct from your benefit, and pay to a provincial or municipal authority, a welfare payment it made for a period for which your benefit is later paid.
@export How much may the Minister deduct from my benefit to repay a provincial or municipal authority (s 65(2))?
GIVEN `an authority paid me an advance or welfare for a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a provincial or municipal authority pay you an advance, assistance or welfare payment for a month or part of a month?
      `it would not have been paid had my benefit been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would that payment not have been paid if a benefit under the Act had been paid for that period?
      `a benefit is now payable for that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a benefit now become payable, or may payment of a benefit be made, to you for that period?
      `the amount the authority paid me` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the authority pay you, in dollars?
      `my benefit for that period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the benefit payable to you for that period, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much may the Minister deduct from my benefit to repay a provincial or municipal authority` IS
    `s 65(2) — the most the Minister may deduct from the benefit and pay to the provincial or municipal authority` `an authority paid me an advance or welfare for a period` `it would not have been paid had my benefit been paid` `a benefit is now payable for that period` `the amount the authority paid me` `my benefit for that period`

-- s 65(3). The Minister may deduct from a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit, and pay to an approved administrator, a payment the administrator made for a period for which you are later paid.
@export How much may the Minister deduct from my disability benefit to repay a disability income program (s 65(3))?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A `Kind of benefit` @desc Which benefit is it: a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit (or another)?
      `the administrator is approved by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the administrator of the disability income program approved by the Minister?
      `the program paid me for a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the program pay you for a month or part of a month a payment that would not have been made if a benefit under paragraph 44(1)(b) or (h) had been paid to you for that period?
      `a benefit is now payable for that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a benefit now become payable, or may payment of a benefit be made, to you for that period?
      `the administrator sent a record and my irrevocable written consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the administrator send the Minister a record of the payment together with your irrevocable written consent to the deduction and payment?
      `the Minister received those documents within a year of my consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were those documents received by the Minister within one year after the date you signed the consent?
      `the amount the program paid me` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the program pay you, in dollars?
      `my benefit for that period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the benefit payable to you for that period, in dollars?
      `no other deduction has been authorized for that payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that no other deduction and payment has already been authorized in respect of that payment?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much may the Minister deduct from my disability benefit to repay a disability income program` IS
    `s 65(3) — the most the Minister may deduct from the benefit and pay to the administrator of a disability income program` `the benefit` `the administrator is approved by the Minister` `the program paid me for a period` `a benefit is now payable for that period` `the administrator sent a record and my irrevocable written consent` `the Minister received those documents within a year of my consent` `the amount the program paid me` `my benefit for that period` `no other deduction has been authorized for that payment`

§§ `Assigning part of my retirement pension to my spouse or partner (section 65.1) -- ask only if you or your spouse or common-law partner want part of a retirement pension assigned`

-- s 65.1(4). A clause in your agreement that expressly mentions the Act and says there is to be no assignment binds the Minister.
@export Does our agreement stop the Minister approving an assignment (s 65.1(4))?
GIVEN `the day we entered into our written agreement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you and your spouse or partner enter into your written agreement?
      `it expressly mentions the Act and says there is to be no assignment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement contain a provision that expressly mentions the Canada Pension Plan Act and says there is to be no assignment under section 65.1?
      `provincial law expressly permits that provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that provision expressly permitted under the provincial law that governs such agreements?
      `the day of the application for the assignment` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the application for the assignment made?
      `a court has invalidated that provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that provision been invalidated by a court order?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our agreement stop the Minister approving an assignment` IS
    `s 65.1(4) — a provision of the agreement binds the Minister, who shall not approve an assignment` `the day we entered into our written agreement` `it expressly mentions the Act and says there is to be no assignment` `provincial law expressly permits that provision` `the day of the application for the assignment` `a court has invalidated that provision`

-- s 65.1(3). Other agreement or court order provisions made on or after 4 June 1986 do not bind the Minister.
@export Do the provisions of our agreement or court order bind the Minister on an assignment (s 65.1(3))?
GIVEN `the day the agreement was entered into or the order made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the agreement entered into or the court order made?
      `subsection (4) applies to a provision of our agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 65.1(4) apply to a provision of the agreement (see the question about agreements)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the provisions of our agreement or court order bind the Minister on an assignment` IS
    `s 65.1(3) — the provisions of the agreement or court order are not binding on the Minister` `the day the agreement was entered into or the order made` `subsection (4) applies to a provision of our agreement`

-- s 65.1(6), (7). Which retirement pensions an assignment covers.
@export Which retirement pensions would an assignment cover (s 65.1(6), (7))?
GIVEN `a retirement pension is payable to both of us under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a retirement pension payable to both you and your spouse or common-law partner under the Act?
      `one under the Act and the other under a provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a retirement pension payable to one of you under the Act and to the other under a provincial pension plan?
      `an agreement under section 80 provides for an assignment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an agreement under section 80 provide for an assignment in that case?
      `only one of us is a contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one of you a contributor under the Act and the other not a contributor under the Act or a provincial pension plan?
      `a retirement pension is payable to the contributor under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a retirement pension payable to the contributor under the Act?
      `the non-contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is the non-contributor's date of birth?
      `the day the age is tested` IS A DATE @desc On what day should the non-contributor's age be tested (usually the day of the application)?
GIVETH A `cp4 Pensions an assignment covers`
DECIDE `Which retirement pensions would an assignment cover` IS
    `s 65.1(6) and (7) — the pensions the assignment is made in respect of` (`s 65.1(6) — the circumstances of a double assignment exist` `a retirement pension is payable to both of us under the Act` `one under the Act and the other under a provincial plan` `an agreement under section 80 provides for an assignment`) (`s 65.1(7) — the circumstances of a single assignment exist` `only one of us is a contributor` `a retirement pension is payable to the contributor under the Act` `the non-contributor's date of birth` `the day the age is tested`)

-- s 65.1(1), (5). The Minister may approve an assignment on your application if the circumstances exist and no binding agreement stops it, and must tell the other spouse or partner of the application.
@export May the Minister approve the assignment of part of my retirement pension (s 65.1(1))?
GIVEN `an application has been made in the prescribed manner and form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made in the prescribed manner and form by the contributor or by the spouse or common-law partner?
      `the circumstances of subsection (6) or (7) exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the circumstances of a double or a single assignment exist (see the question about which pensions an assignment covers)?
      `our agreement binds the Minister under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of an agreement bind the Minister under subsection 65.1(4)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister approve the assignment of part of my retirement pension` IS
    `s 65.1(1) — the Minister may approve the assignment` `an application has been made in the prescribed manner and form` `the circumstances of subsection (6) or (7) exist` `our agreement binds the Minister under subsection (4)`

@export Must the Minister tell my spouse or partner that I have applied for an assignment (s 65.1(5))?
GIVEN `I have applied for an assignment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for an assignment of your spouse's or common-law partner's retirement pension?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister tell my spouse or partner that I have applied for an assignment` IS
    `s 65.1(5) — the Minister must at once notify the other spouse or common-law partner` `I have applied for an assignment`

-- s 65.1(8). Months in the joint contributory period (base), the first and second additional ones, and the period of cohabitation.
@export How many months are in our joint contributory period (s 65.1(8))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `my spouse's or partner's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your spouse's or common-law partner's date of birth?
      `we are both contributors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you both contributors?
      `the month the later of our contributory periods ends` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the later of your contributory periods end (any date in it)?
      `the month the contributor's contributory period ends` IS A DATE @desc If only one of you is a contributor, in which month does the contributor's contributory period end (any date in it)?
      `the non-contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc If only one of you is a contributor, what is the non-contributor's date of birth?
      `the month the assignment application is approved` IS A DATE @desc In which month is the application for the assignment approved (any date in it)?
      `subsection (6) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a retirement pension payable to both of you (or the case of subsection 65.1(6))?
      `months excluded from both our contributory periods` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are excluded from the contributory period of both of you under paragraph 49(c) or (d)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months are in our joint contributory period` IS
    `s 65.1(8) — the number of months in the joint contributory period` `my date of birth` `my spouse's or partner's date of birth` `we are both contributors` `the month the later of our contributory periods ends` `the month the contributor's contributory period ends` `the non-contributor's date of birth` `the month the assignment application is approved` `subsection (6) applies` `months excluded from both our contributory periods`

@export How many months are in our first additional joint contributory period (s 65.1(8))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `my spouse's or partner's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your spouse's or common-law partner's date of birth?
      `we are both contributors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you both contributors?
      `the month the later of our first additional contributory periods ends` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the later of your first additional contributory periods end (any date in it)?
      `the month the contributor's first additional contributory period ends` IS A DATE @desc If only one of you is a contributor, in which month does the contributor's first additional contributory period end (any date in it)?
      `the non-contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc If only one of you is a contributor, what is the non-contributor's date of birth?
      `the month the assignment application is approved` IS A DATE @desc In which month is the application for the assignment approved (any date in it)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months are in our first additional joint contributory period` IS
    `s 65.1(8) — the number of months in the first additional joint contributory period` `my date of birth` `my spouse's or partner's date of birth` `we are both contributors` `the month the later of our first additional contributory periods ends` `the month the contributor's first additional contributory period ends` `the non-contributor's date of birth` `the month the assignment application is approved`

@export How many months are in our second additional joint contributory period (s 65.1(8))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `my spouse's or partner's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your spouse's or common-law partner's date of birth?
      `we are both contributors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you both contributors?
      `the month the later of our second additional contributory periods ends` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the later of your second additional contributory periods end (any date in it)?
      `the month the contributor's second additional contributory period ends` IS A DATE @desc If only one of you is a contributor, in which month does the contributor's second additional contributory period end (any date in it)?
      `the non-contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc If only one of you is a contributor, what is the non-contributor's date of birth?
      `the month the assignment application is approved` IS A DATE @desc In which month is the application for the assignment approved (any date in it)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months are in our second additional joint contributory period` IS
    `s 65.1(8) — the number of months in the second additional joint contributory period` `my date of birth` `my spouse's or partner's date of birth` `we are both contributors` `the month the later of our second additional contributory periods ends` `the month the contributor's second additional contributory period ends` `the non-contributor's date of birth` `the month the assignment application is approved`

@export How many months are in our period of cohabitation (s 65.1(8))?
GIVEN `the month we married or began to live together` IS A DATE @desc In which month were you married or did you start to live together in a conjugal relationship (any date in it)?
      `the last month we lived together` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you last live together (any date in it)?
      `the first month of our joint contributory period` IS A DATE @desc In which month does your joint contributory period begin (any date in it)?
      `the last month of our joint contributory period` IS A DATE @desc In which month does your joint contributory period end (any date in it)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months are in our period of cohabitation` IS
    `s 65.1(8) — the number of months in the period of cohabitation` `the month we married or began to live together` `the last month we lived together` `the first month of our joint contributory period` `the last month of our joint contributory period`

-- s 65.1(9). The portion assigned is 50% of each portion of the contributor's retirement pension, weighted by months of cohabitation over months of joint contributory period.
@export What portion of the contributor's retirement pension is assigned to the spouse or partner (s 65.1(9))?
GIVEN `the base portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the portion of the contributor's retirement pension under paragraph 46(1)(a), adjusted under section 45, in dollars a month?
      `the first additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the portion under paragraph 46(1)(b), adjusted under section 45, in dollars a month?
      `the second additional portion` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the portion under paragraph 46(1)(c), adjusted under section 45, in dollars a month?
      `months of cohabitation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in the period of cohabitation?
      `months in the joint contributory period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in the joint contributory period?
      `months in the first additional joint contributory period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in the first additional joint contributory period?
      `months in the second additional joint contributory period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in the second additional joint contributory period?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What portion of the contributor's retirement pension is assigned to the spouse or partner` IS
    `s 65.1(9) — the portion of the contributor's retirement pension to be assigned` (`cp4 Retirement pension portions` WITH
        `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension` IS `the base portion`
        `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `the first additional portion`
        `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension` IS `the second additional portion`) `months of cohabitation` `months in the joint contributory period` `months in the first additional joint contributory period` `months in the second additional joint contributory period`

-- s 65.1(10), (11), (11.1), (11.2), (12). The assignment starts the month after approval and stops at the earliest of the listed events; either spouse can ask to have a cancelled assignment reinstated; both must be notified.
@export In which month does the assignment commence (s 65.1(10))?
GIVEN `the month the application for the assignment is approved` IS A DATE @desc In which month is the application for the assignment approved (any date in it)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `In which month does the assignment commence` IS
    `s 65.1(10) — the month with which the assignment commences` `the month the application for the assignment is approved`

@export In which month does the assignment cease (s 65.1(11))?
GIVEN `one of us has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has either of you died?
      `the day one of us died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that happen? (Any date if not)
      `we have separated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you commenced to live separate and apart within the meaning of paragraphs 55.1(2)(a) and (b)?
      `the day we separated` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that happen? (Any date if not)
      `subsection (7) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assignment one under subsection 65.1(7) (only one of you a contributor)?
      `the non-contributor has become a contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the non-contributor become a contributor?
      `the day the non-contributor became a contributor` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that happen? (Any date if not)
      `a divorce or nullity has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a decree absolute of divorce, a judgment granting a divorce under the Divorce Act or a judgment of nullity of the marriage been issued?
      `the day it was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it issued? (Any date if not)
      `we asked for the assignment to be cancelled and the Minister approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved a request in writing from both of you that the assignment be cancelled?
      `the day the Minister approved the cancellation` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that happen? (Any date if not)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `In which month does the assignment cease` IS
    `s 65.1(11) — the month with which the assignment ceases` (`when it happened` `one of us has died` `the day one of us died`) (`when it happened` `we have separated` `the day we separated`) `subsection (7) applies` (`when it happened` `the non-contributor has become a contributor` `the day the non-contributor became a contributor`) (`when it happened` `a divorce or nullity has been issued` `the day it was issued`) (`when it happened` `we asked for the assignment to be cancelled and the Minister approved` `the day the Minister approved the cancellation`)
    WHERE
        `when it happened` happened day MEANS IF happened THEN JUST day ELSE NOTHING

@export May either of us ask in writing for the cancelled assignment to be reinstated (s 65.1(11.1))?
GIVEN `the assignment ceased because the Minister approved our request to cancel it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the assignment cease under paragraph 65.1(11)(e), because the Minister approved your written request to cancel it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May either of us ask in writing for the cancelled assignment to be reinstated` IS
    `s 65.1(11.1) — either spouse or either common-law partner may request in writing that the assignment be reinstated` `the assignment ceased because the Minister approved our request to cancel it`

@export On what day is the assignment reinstated (s 65.1(11.2))?
GIVEN `the day the Minister approves the request for reinstatement` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the Minister approve the request for reinstatement?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day is the assignment reinstated` IS
    `s 65.1(11.2) — the day the assignment is reinstated` `the day the Minister approves the request for reinstatement`

@export Must we both be notified when the Minister approves the assignment (s 65.1(12))?
GIVEN `the Minister has approved an assignment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved the assignment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we both be notified when the Minister approves the assignment` IS
    `s 65.1(12) — both spouses or both common-law partners must be notified` `the Minister has approved an assignment`
§§ `Overpayments, recovery and official error (section 66) -- ask only if you were paid a benefit you were not entitled to, or the Minister's error cost you a benefit`

-- s 66(1), (2). You must at once return a benefit payment you were not entitled to, or the excess; the amount is a debt to the Crown.
@export How much of a benefit payment must I return at once (s 66(1))?
GIVEN `the amount I received` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the benefit payment did you receive or obtain, in dollars?
      `the amount I am entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of it were you entitled to, in dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of a benefit payment must I return at once` IS
    `s 66(1) — the amount the person or estate must at once return` `the amount I received` `the amount I am entitled to`

@export Is the overpaid amount a debt I owe to the Crown that can be recovered at any time (s 66(2))?
GIVEN `the amount I received` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the benefit payment did you receive or obtain, in dollars?
      `the amount I am entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of it were you entitled to, in dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the overpaid amount a debt I owe to the Crown that can be recovered at any time` IS
    `s 66(2) — the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable at any time` `the amount I received` `the amount I am entitled to`

-- s 66(2.01), (2.02). Interest payable under Part II, and a penalty under section 90.1, are debts to the Crown too.
@export Is the interest I owe under this Part a debt to the Crown (s 66(2.01))?
GIVEN `the amount is interest payable under Part II` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount interest payable under Part II of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the interest I owe under this Part a debt to the Crown` IS
    `s 66(2.01) — the interest is a debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable at any time` `the amount is interest payable under Part II`

@export Is a penalty imposed on me under section 90.1 a debt to the Crown (s 66(2.02))?
GIVEN `the amount is a penalty imposed on me under section 90.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount a penalty imposed on you under section 90.1?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a penalty imposed on me under section 90.1 a debt to the Crown` IS
    `s 66(2.02) — the penalty is a debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable at any time` `the amount is a penalty imposed on me under section 90.1`

-- s 66(2.1). What I owe may be deducted and retained out of other amounts payable to me, by regulation 42 without undue hardship.
@export How much may be deducted from other amounts payable to me to recover what I owe (s 66(2.1))?
GIVEN `what I owe` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you owe, in dollars?
      `what is payable to me` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is payable to you under the Act or any other Act or program the Minister administers, in dollars?
      `the most that can be deducted without undue hardship to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the most that can be deducted without causing you undue hardship, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much may be deducted from other amounts payable to me to recover what I owe` IS
    `s 66(2.1) — the most that may be deducted and retained out of an amount payable` `what I owe` `what is payable to me` `the most that can be deducted without undue hardship to me`

-- s 66(2.2). The Minister may certify what has not been recovered at once if you appear to be avoiding payment, otherwise once 30 days after the default have expired.
@export On what day may the Minister first certify what I owe (s 66(2.2))?
GIVEN `the Minister thinks I am trying to avoid payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it, in the Minister's opinion, that you are attempting to avoid payment?
      `the day the Minister formed that opinion` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Minister form that opinion? (Any date if not)
      `the day I defaulted` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you default on the debt?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day may the Minister first certify what I owe` IS
    `s 66(2.2) — the first day on which the Minister may certify the indebtedness that has not been recovered` `the Minister thinks I am trying to avoid payment` `the day the Minister formed that opinion` `the day I defaulted`

-- s 66(2.3) to (2.6). A registered certificate is enforceable as a Federal Court judgment, may be registered in the provincial superior court, carries costs, and may be recorded against your land.
@export Does the registered certificate have the force of a Federal Court judgment against me (s 66(2.3))?
GIVEN `the certificate has been registered in the Federal Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister's certificate been produced to, and registered in, the Federal Court?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the registered certificate have the force of a Federal Court judgment against me` IS
    `s 66(2.3) — the registered certificate has the force and effect of a judgment of the Federal Court for a debt` `the certificate has been registered in the Federal Court`

@export May the certificate also be registered in the superior court of my province (s 66(2.4))?
GIVEN `the certificate has been registered in the Federal Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certificate been registered in the Federal Court?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the certificate also be registered in the superior court of my province` IS
    `s 66(2.4) — the certificate may also be registered in the superior court of a province` `the certificate has been registered in the Federal Court`

@export Can the reasonable costs of registering the certificate be recovered from me (s 66(2.5))?
GIVEN `the costs are reasonable and are for registering the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the costs and charges reasonable and for the registration of the certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the reasonable costs of registering the certificate be recovered from me` IS
    `s 66(2.5) — the costs and charges are recoverable as if certified and the certificate registered` `the costs are reasonable and are for registering the certificate`

@export Can the certificate be recorded as a charge on my land (s 66(2.6))?
GIVEN `the certificate has been registered in a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a certificate in respect of you been registered in the Federal Court or a superior court?
      `a court document evidencing the certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Federal Court or the superior court issued a document evidencing the certificate?
      `I hold or own land or an interest in land in a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold or own land, or an interest in land, in a province?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the certificate be recorded as a charge on my land` IS
    `s 66(2.6) — the document may be recorded to create security, a charge, lien or legal hypothec on the debtor's land` `the certificate has been registered in a court` `a court document evidencing the certificate has been issued` `I hold or own land or an interest in land in a province`

-- s 66(2.7), (2.8), (2.9). The Minister may require someone who owes money to the debtor to pay it to the Receiver General; if they do not, the amount is a debt to the Crown; an affidavit proves personal service.
@export Can I be required to pay money I owe to a debtor of the Crown to the Receiver General (s 66(2.7))?
GIVEN `the Minister knows or suspects I owe money to a person who owes the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister know or suspect that you are or are about to become indebted, or liable to make a payment, to a person liable to make a payment to Her Majesty under this Part?
      `the Minister served a notice on me personally or by confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a notice served on you personally or by confirmed delivery service?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be required to pay money I owe to a debtor of the Crown to the Receiver General` IS
    `s 66(2.7) — the person is required to pay the money otherwise payable to the debtor to the Receiver General` `the Minister knows or suspects I owe money to a person who owes the Crown` `the Minister served a notice on me personally or by confirmed delivery service`

@export Is an amount I did not pay as the Minister's notice required a debt I owe to the Crown (s 66(2.8))?
GIVEN `the notice required me to pay an amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a notice under subsection 66(2.7) require you to pay an amount?
      `I did not pay it as the notice required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not pay the amount as the notice required?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an amount I did not pay as the Minister's notice required a debt I owe to the Crown` IS
    `s 66(2.8) — the amount not paid as required by the notice is a debt due to Her Majesty` `the notice required me to pay an amount` `I did not pay it as the notice required`

@export Is an affidavit of service proof that the Minister's notice was served on me (s 66(2.9))?
GIVEN `the Act or regulations provide for personal service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act or the regulations provide for personal service of the request, notice or demand?
      `the affiant has charge of the records and knows the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that the person who served it has charge of the appropriate records and knowledge of the facts?
      `it was served personally on a named day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state it was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed?
      `a true copy is attached as an exhibit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit identify as an exhibit a true copy of the request, notice or demand?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an affidavit of service proof that the Minister's notice was served on me` IS
    `s 66(2.9) — the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` `the Act or regulations provide for personal service` `the affiant has charge of the records and knows the facts` `it was served personally on a named day` `a true copy is attached as an exhibit`

-- s 66(3). The Minister may remit what you owe if it cannot be collected, costs more to collect, would cause you undue hardship, or resulted from official error, unless you were convicted in connection with the payment.
@export May the Minister remit what I owe (s 66(3))?
GIVEN `I was overpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive or obtain a benefit payment to which you were not entitled, or in excess of what you were entitled to?
      `the Minister is satisfied it cannot be collected in the foreseeable future` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the amount cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future?
      `the Minister is satisfied it will cost as much to collect as the amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the administrative costs of collecting it are likely to equal or exceed the amount?
      `the Minister is satisfied repayment would cause me undue hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that repayment would cause you undue hardship?
      `the Minister is satisfied it resulted from official error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that it resulted from erroneous advice or administrative error on the part of the Minister or an official of the Department of Employment and Social Development?
      `I was convicted in connection with obtaining it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of an offence under the Act or of the Criminal Code in connection with obtaining the payment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister remit what I owe` IS
    `s 66(3) — the Minister may remit all or any portion of the amount or excess` `I was overpaid` `the Minister is satisfied it cannot be collected in the foreseeable future` `the Minister is satisfied it will cost as much to collect as the amount` `the Minister is satisfied repayment would cause me undue hardship` `the Minister is satisfied it resulted from official error` `I was convicted in connection with obtaining it`

-- s 66(4), (5). The Minister must put right the effect of erroneous advice or administrative error, including a division denied under an old agreement.
@export Must the Minister put me back in the position I would be in if official error denied me a benefit, division or assignment (s 66(4))?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that official error denied me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that, as a result of erroneous advice or administrative error in the administration of the Act, you were denied something below?
      `a benefit or part of one I was entitled to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you denied a benefit, or a portion of one, to which you would have been entitled?
      `a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you denied a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1?
      `an assignment of a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you denied an assignment of a retirement pension under section 65.1?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister put me back in the position I would be in if official error denied me a benefit, division or assignment` IS
    `s 66(4) — the Minister must take remedial action to place the person in the position the person would be in` `the Minister is satisfied that official error denied me` `a benefit or part of one I was entitled to` `a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` `an assignment of a retirement pension`

@export Must the Minister put right a division I was denied under an agreement or order made before 4 June 1986 (s 66(5))?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied I was denied a division by an agreement or order made before 4 June 1986` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that you were denied a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1 as a result of a written agreement entered into, or a court order made, before 4 June 1986?
      `the agreement or order does not say there be no division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement or order not indicate that there be no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under the Act?
      `all the other criteria for a division are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the other criteria specified by or under the Act respecting divisions met?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister put right a division I was denied under an agreement or order made before 4 June 1986` IS
    `s 66(5) — the Minister must take remedial action, including attributing the earnings that would have been attributed` `the Minister is satisfied I was denied a division by an agreement or order made before 4 June 1986` `the agreement or order does not say there be no division` `all the other criteria for a division are met`

-- s 66(6). Section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act does not apply to amounts owing under this Part.
@export Does section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act apply to what I owe under this Part (s 66(6))?
GIVEN `the amount is owing to the Crown under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount owing to Her Majesty under Part II of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act apply to what I owe under this Part` IS
    `s 66(6) — section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act applies in relation to the amount` `the amount is owing to the Crown under this Part`

§§ `Cancelling a benefit (section 66.1) -- ask only if you want to cancel a benefit you have started to receive`

-- s 66.1(1), (1.1). A beneficiary may, in writing and within 12 months after payment began (regulation 46.2(1)), ask to cancel a benefit; not a retirement pension in favour of a disability benefit where you were disabled in or after the month it first became payable.
@export May I ask to cancel my benefit (s 66.1(1), (1.1))?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A `Kind of benefit` @desc Which benefit do you want to cancel?
      `the day my payments began` IS A DATE @desc On what date did payment of the benefit begin?
      `the day I make the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make the request?
      `I make the request in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make the request in the prescribed manner (in writing to the Minister)?
      `I have applied for a disability benefit and receive a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for a disability benefit under the Act or a provincial pension plan, and are you in receipt of a retirement pension?
      `the month I am deemed to have become disabled` IS A DATE @desc In which month are you deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of entitlement to the disability benefit (any date in it; any date if not applicable)?
      `the month my retirement pension first became payable` IS A DATE @desc For which month did your retirement pension first become payable (any date in it)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask to cancel my benefit` IS
    `s 66.1(1) — the beneficiary may request cancellation of the benefit` `the day my payments began` `the day I make the request` `I make the request in the prescribed manner` (`s 66.1(1.1) — subsection (1) does not apply to the cancellation of the retirement pension` `the benefit` `I have applied for a disability benefit and receive a retirement pension` `the month I am deemed to have become disabled` `the month my retirement pension first became payable`)

-- s 66.1(2). If the request is granted and you repay what was paid within 12 months after the month it was granted (regulation 46.2(4); or the provincial plan's time), the benefit is treated as never payable.
@export Is my cancelled benefit treated as never having been payable (s 66.1(2))?
GIVEN `my request was granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your request to cancel the benefit, under the Act or a substantially similar provincial provision, granted?
      `my request was under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your request made under a provincial pension plan?
      `the day my request was granted` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it granted?
      `the day I repaid the benefits paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you repay the amount of the benefits paid?
      `I repaid within the time the provincial plan allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was under a provincial plan, did you repay within the time that plan provides?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my cancelled benefit treated as never having been payable` IS
    `s 66.1(2) — the benefit is deemed for all purposes of this Act not to have been payable during the period` `my request was granted` `my request was under a provincial pension plan` `the day my request was granted` `the day I repaid the benefits paid` `I repaid within the time the provincial plan allows`
